 {"id":"DF-OFF-BY-ONE-28","title":"nohup'd serve survives bunker destroy \u2014 agents share host netns so port 8766 is not agent-private; destroyed agent leaves a bound listener","status":"complete","priority":"P3","complexity":1,"reasoning":"Install-proof re-run 2026-10-02 (tick off-by-one-foreman-2026-10-02-10-44-23): after `bunker destroy oby-install-test`, the `nohup ./off-by-one... --port 8766 &` serve kept running on the host (pgrep 1738097) \u2014 the next agent's fresh install then hit a 54m-uptime listener on 'its' localhost:8766, which silently defeats any install-verification probe. Agents on las-bunker-03 run with a shared host network namespace (ports are host-global); bunkerd destroy does not reap agent-spawned background processes. Evidence: docs/dogfood/evidence/2026-10-02-install-bunker-las-03-raw.log (ANOMALY + VERIFIED CLEAN sections; orphans killed via host sudo pkill).","capability_tags":["infra","bunker","dogfood"],"fix_direction":"Either bunkerd destroy kills the agent user's processes (cgroup kill), or agents get per-agent netns/port ranges; short-term: install docs must say 'use an agent-unique port and kill the serve before destroy'. Musterflow-side consumer note: install-leg verification probes must assert uptime is seconds, not just status ok.","commit_hash":"7dd4e6d4","worker_summary":"Worker kimi-k3: docs-only commit 7dd4e6d4 adds 'Port hygiene on shared-host / bunker installs' callout to README.md (agent-unique port, kill serve before bunker destroy, evidence link) and the fresh-uptime /health probe rule to docs/integration.md. No .go files changed; go build ok. Judge PASS 183923dd.","foreman_note":"Tick off-by-one-foreman-2026-10-04-12-38-49: docs-only, single worker dispatch.","updated_at":"2026-10-04T08:05:00-05:00"}
 {"id":"DF-OFF-BY-ONE-29","title":"Idle gate is disabled (-load-threshold -1): the solver runs continuously even when the host is saturated","status":"complete","priority":"P0","complexity":2,"reasoning":"deploy/off-by-one.service:55 ships `-load-threshold -1`, and the binary's own help says \"Max loadavg(1) for idle detection (negative = always idle) (default 1)\". The lab's stated purpose is to convert IDLE cycles into answers, so -1 removes the very gate that keeps it opportunistic. Measured consequence 2026-10-03: with loadavg ~60 and io pressure 95%, the daemon kept dequeueing and launching solves every 60s; an AI-generated Go test (bbr.test) reached 47 GB RSS = 75% of RAM and swap filled to 55.5 GiB of 55 GiB (completely full), TWICE inside twenty minutes. Prometheus on fleet-monitor: node_memory_MemAvailable 44.7 -> 4.1 GiB, node_memory_AnonPages 8.5 -> 49.3 GiB, peak memory pressure some avg10 = 34.9%. Full evidence: ~/reports/ram-incident-2026-10-03/index.html (section 4).","capability_tags":["ops","deploy","config"],"fix_direction":"Restore a real threshold in deploy/off-by-one.service: replace `-load-threshold -1` with a positive value (default 1; o=4 is a defensible start for a 16-core box that also runs the fleet). The repo file is the source of truth \u2014 the host currently carries an ops drop-in with only memory limits, so a redeploy from deploy/ would reintroduce -1. Acceptance: (a) `grep load-threshold deploy/off-by-one.service` shows a positive number; (b) journal shows a skip/back-off line when loadavg(1) >= the threshold, produced by a repro (run a bounded load generator to push loadavg above the threshold and observe no solve starts); (c) the chosen value and the reason are recorded in the repo (unit comment or docs/).","worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"95a66683","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Foreman-direct: restored -load-threshold 4 in deploy/off-by-one.service. Guard DEGRADED PASS. Judge PASS verdict 326588dd. Pushed to origin/master.","updated_at":"2026-10-04T06:12:41Z","completed_at":"2026-10-04T06:12:41Z"}
 {"id":"DF-OFF-BY-ONE-30","title":"No memory bound on AI-written code: one generated test reached 47 GB and filled swap; the repo unit must carry the cap","status":"complete","priority":"P0","complexity":3,"reasoning":"The solver compiles and runs code that an LLM wrote, and nothing in the chain limits its memory: bwrap isolates filesystem/PID/session namespaces but not memory (internal/sandbox/bwrap.go documents exactly that scope), the unit ran MemoryMax=infinity/MemoryHigh=infinity, and the only cap was time (internal/solver/piagent.go: DefaultSolveTimeout = 30 min). On 2026-10-03 a generated test allocated 47 GB in minutes; because swap absorbed it (46 GB, then 55.5 GB = 100% of swap) the kernel never OOM-killed it, so the host thrashed for ~10 minutes instead of failing fast. Ops applied a HOST-ONLY drop-in (/etc/systemd/system/off-by-one.service.d/memory-cap.conf: MemoryHigh=6G, MemoryMax=8G, MemorySwapMax=2G, verified effective) \u2014 but that is not in the repo and will not survive a redeploy.","capability_tags":["ops","deploy","sandbox","tooling"],"fix_direction":"Make the bound durable and per-solve: (a) add MemoryHigh/MemoryMax/MemorySwapMax to deploy/off-by-one.service so a redeploy cannot ship an uncapped solver; (b) cap each solve individually (e.g. run the sandbox under `systemd-run --scope -p MemoryMax=<cap>` or set RLIMIT_AS in internal/sandbox config) so one bad problem cannot consume the daemon's whole budget; (c) surface the kill \u2014 a cgroup OOM kill of a generated test must produce a clear log line naming the problem id. Acceptance: a deliberate runaway fixture (test that allocates unboundedly) is killed at the cap with a named log line, the daemon survives it, and host MemAvailable stays above a floor for the whole test; verified by a self-test that runs that fixture and asserts the kill + the log line.","worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"c48b8979","guard_result":"PASS","completed_at":"2026-10-04 01:20:00","updated_at":"2026-10-04 01:20:00","worker_summary":"Adopted the orphaned 2026-10-03 work (sandbox memcap committed in c1deec5f but the wrapper/flag/unit wiring was uncommitted, worker dead): oby-memcap exec wrapper (1cbf17ca), -solve-mem-mb flag + durable 6G/8G/2G unit caps (c48b8979), and the judge-required kernel-level inheritance test TestObyMemcapExec_ChildInheritsCap (real wrapper exec -> /proc/self/limits soft==hard 67108864 bytes). Judge FAIL 3fa7b03f -> PASS 6b352678. Full suite green; repo-wide golangci-lint 0. Binary rebuilt+redeployed (kill MainPID -> Restart=always, fresh PID 2286235->). NOTE: host unit /etc/systemd/system/off-by-one.service ExecStart still lacks -solve-mem-mb 6144 (approval-gated); the 8G cgroup drop-in caps ARE live. DF-29 (load-threshold 4) landed by a sibling tick (ef7b6b63/fc8b9364).","foreman_note":"tick off-by-one-foreman-2026-10-04-05-44-08: adopted orphaned in-progress work, judged PASS, deployed."}
-{"id":"DF-OFF-BY-ONE-31","title":"Generated solution accumulates per-event slices with no bound \u2014 the 47 GB allocation is in the solved code, not the harness","status":"complete","priority":"P1","complexity":3,"reasoning":"The runaway was not the daemon (live cgroup 0.26 GB after the test exited) \u2014 it was the generated packet-level simulator. In the sandbox for problem class go-bbr-pacing-congestion-bandwidth-delay-probe (problem.json, 11:02) the agent wrote bbr/bbr.go (425 lines), bbr/sim.go (309 lines) and two *_test.go files; sim.go appends once per simulated event and never trims: sim.go:189 `s.queueAt = append(s.queueAt, QueuePoint{...})` and sim.go:106 `s.lossPlan = append(s.lossPlan, lossInjection{...})`. A deep-buffer bottleneck with a scripted ACK trace generates an unbounded number of events, so memory scales with simulated packets. The agent itself added an iteration guard in the test (debug_test.go:30 `if count > 5000000`) \u2014 evidence it already knew the loop could run away. Host-capping this (DF-OFF-BY-ONE-30) stops the blast radius but does not fix a solver that produces unbounded simulations.","capability_tags":["solver","sandbox","tooling","ci"],"fix_direction":"Bound the work the solver is allowed to produce, at both ends. Prompt side: require that solutions to simulation classes declare their bounds (max simulated events/packets/seconds) and aggregate incrementally instead of retaining a record per event; state a memory budget the generated tests must respect. Harness side: measure the peak RSS of each test run and treat a run that approaches the cap as a rejected answer (with the measured number recorded against the problem id), so a rejected problem produces a finding rather than a host incident. Acceptance: (a) an unbounded simulation fixture is REJECTED by the harness with its measured peak recorded; (b) a bounded version of the same problem is accepted and verified; (c) the prompt/contract change is asserted by a test so it cannot silently regress.","worker_status":"complete","completed_at":"2026-10-04T13:35:00Z","commit_hash":"6c354615","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Worker deepseek-v4-flash: harness-side near-cap rejection (-solve-reject-rss-mb, default auto=80% of -solve-mem-mb, 0=disabled) with measured peak in failure reason + SolveRejected metric + Rejected in SolveRecord/observer; pi-agent bounds contract (declare explicit max events/packets/seconds, aggregate incrementally); docs/api-reference.md section. AC tests: TestLoopRejectsNearCapSolve (a), TestLoopAcceptsBoundedSolveBelowRejectThreshold (b), TestPiAgentWrapperDeclaresResourceBounds (c) all pass; go build/vet/golangci-lint clean, full suite ok. Merged ff to master 6c354615, pushed, 0 unpushed. Judge FAIL ead89580 (ran before merge, correct) superseded by PASS ce21623d on merged tip.","foreman_note":"Tick off-by-one-foreman-2026-10-04-12-38-49. ch:trace row=DF-OFF-BY-ONE-31 spec=docs/api-reference.md#solve-memory-bounds witness=commit:6c354615 verdict=ce21623d evidence=internal/cron/memgate_test.go::TestLoopRejectsNearCapSolve commit=6c354615"}
