 {"id":"PII-OB-001","title":"[P1] Redact common personal data from every shared-answer surface by default","status":"complete","priority":"P1","type":"task","created_by":"off-by-one-foreman","created_at":"2026-10-06T07:24:01Z","reasoning":"Agent-generated diagnostics can contain personal home-directory paths, email addresses, phone numbers, and host IP addresses. The repo corpus is intentionally public and the read-only catalog publishes answer records; gitleaks allowlists corpus content because it also contains dummy credentials, so it is not a general PII detector. Planned fix: Apply one documented default redaction policy to the flat corpus export, Git subtree answer export, and read-only public JSON responses. Cover Linux/macOS/Windows home paths, emails, phone numbers, IPv4 and IPv6. Use neutral placeholders, preserve non-string JSON fields and surrounding technical content, and fail closed if safe serialization is impossible.","acceptance_criteria":"(1) Every exported free-text field and nested signatures value/key is scrubbed for personal home paths, email, phone, IPv4, and IPv6. (2) The public read-only API applies the same scrub to all JSON responses, including discovery, answers, taxonomy and queue metadata. (3) Unit and live-handler tests prove raw fixture PII is absent and placeholders remain. (4) Existing corpus content is regenerated from the operational DB through the sanitizer; counts/answer identities remain stable.","completed_at":"2026-10-06T19:05:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T19:05:00Z","commit_hash":"8d3d7924","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Verification-only close (flip-miss repair): commit 8d3d7924 (2026-10-06 02:58, ~30min after filing) implements this row. Verified this tick: (a) export sanitizer sanitize_common_pii in scripts/export-answers.py (home paths/email/phone/IPv4/IPv6 -> neutral placeholders) applied to flat corpus + git subtree + nested signatures; corpus regenerated, counts stable (data/COUNTS.md 2526 classes / 4153 answers); (b) read-only public API scrub via sanitizeReadOnlyJSON wrapper (internal/api/server.go:116-136) + TestReadOnly_PublicJSONRedactsCommonPII passing; (c) scripts/check-public-pii.py wired into corpus hygiene (check-corpus-hygiene.sh:81), failure output reports category/file/count only; self-test 45/45 green incl. email/phone/IPv4/IPv6 fixture arms; (d) CI green on 8d3d7924 (run 37433622425). TestSanitizeCommonPII (internal/export) passes. ch:trace row=PII-OB-001 spec=scripts/check-public-pii.py evidence=commit:8d3d7924+CI:37433622425 witness=path@origin:scripts/tests/check-corpus-hygiene-selftest.sh"}
 {"id":"PII-OB-002","title":"[P1] Add a fail-closed, value-safe PII gate for the public corpus and static site","status":"complete","priority":"P1","type":"task","created_by":"off-by-one-foreman","created_at":"2026-10-06T07:24:01Z","reasoning":"Credential scanning alone cannot detect personal paths/contact details/IPs, and the public corpus is intentionally exempted from gitleaks credential rules. A missing privacy check lets future agent output republish private workstation context without stopping CI. Planned fix: Add a dedicated corpus/site checker to the existing CI hygiene job. It must parse structured JSON, inspect generated HTML, reject personal user paths from common OS layouts plus email/phone/IPv4/IPv6, print only category/file/count (never matched values), and have non-vacuous positive/negative fixture arms.","acceptance_criteria":"(1) The current regenerated data/ and site/ pass the gate. (2) Separate fixtures for Windows and escaped Unix paths, email, phone, IPv4, and IPv6 each fail the gate. (3) Redacted placeholders pass. (4) Failure output does not echo any matched PII value. (5) The existing CI corpus-hygiene job invokes the checker and fails on its nonzero status.","completed_at":"2026-10-06T19:05:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T19:05:00Z","commit_hash":"8d3d7924","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Verification-only close (flip-miss repair): commit 8d3d7924 (2026-10-06 02:58, ~30min after filing) implements this row. Verified this tick: (a) export sanitizer sanitize_common_pii in scripts/export-answers.py (home paths/email/phone/IPv4/IPv6 -> neutral placeholders) applied to flat corpus + git subtree + nested signatures; corpus regenerated, counts stable (data/COUNTS.md 2526 classes / 4153 answers); (b) read-only public API scrub via sanitizeReadOnlyJSON wrapper (internal/api/server.go:116-136) + TestReadOnly_PublicJSONRedactsCommonPII passing; (c) scripts/check-public-pii.py wired into corpus hygiene (check-corpus-hygiene.sh:81), failure output reports category/file/count only; self-test 45/45 green incl. email/phone/IPv4/IPv6 fixture arms; (d) CI green on 8d3d7924 (run 37433622425). TestSanitizeCommonPII (internal/export) passes. ch:trace row=PII-OB-002 spec=scripts/check-public-pii.py evidence=commit:8d3d7924+CI:37433622425 witness=path@origin:scripts/tests/check-corpus-hygiene-selftest.sh"}
