 {"id":"INT-CI-003","title":"[P1] CI flake recurrence: TestApplyMemLimitMB_RefusesAllocationPastCap panics on runner (run 37460341755 at 0f1faf30) \u2014 helper child applies RLIMIT_AS=64MiB to a live Go runtime; any subsequent Go runtime allocation (persistentalloc in fmt) throws fatal error: runtime: cannot allocate memory before the mmap(256MiB) ENOMEM probe is reached. The OB-CI-001 watch-only close said escalate on recurrence \u2014 this is the recurrence.","status":"complete","priority":"P1","type":"task","created_by":"off-by-one-foreman","created_at":"2026-10-06T18:20:00Z","reasoning":"Second occurrence family (first: OB-CI-001 watch-only). Evidence: /tmp/oby-fail-job.log line 19757; stack shows runtime.persistentalloc1 \u2192 fatal error under 64MiB RLIMIT_AS. Fix direction: make the under-cap arm assert ENOMEM on an allocation path that does not require a live Go runtime after setrlimit \u2014 e.g. fork a non-Go child (sh -c dd/mmap via python3?) or re-exec with the cap applied via exec-time RLIMIT_AS (syscall before Go heap warm-up is fine; the problem is setrlimit AFTER runtime start). Simplest robust design: helper applies the limit at exec time via a wrapper (prlimit) or the test asserts ApplyMemLimitMB(64) itself succeeds then verifies the 256MiB mmap fails in a process that was launched WITH the limit pre-applied. Alternatively skip/scale when post-setrlimit Go allocation is observed to fail (env-dependent guard).","acceptance_criteria":"(1) The under-cap arm passes deterministically on GitHub runners \u2014 no panic from Go runtime allocation after setrlimit. (2) The test still proves ApplyMemLimitMB enforces a real refusal (ENOMEM observed, not vacuously skipped). (3) Full local suite green; CI Go 1.26 job green on a master push.","completed_at":"2026-10-06T19:05:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T19:05:00Z","commit_hash":"c8c1fe58","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Worker kimi-k3 commit 7cb52cb3 (wt/INT-CI-003 merged to master c8c1fe58): alloc-under-cap arm now syscall.Exec's a non-Go python3 -S probe (resolved pre-cap via OBY_TEST_MEMCAP_PY) for the 256MiB mmap ENOMEM observation - no Go runtime allocation after ApplyMemLimitMB(64). Non-vacuous: uncapped probe prints 'cap not enforced' and exits 1; control arm unchanged and mandatory. Judge COMPLETE job-5cbbe2dc; CI run 37512285601 green 6/6 on c8c1fe58 (pre-fix run 37510484624 reproduced the exact persistentalloc1 panic).","foreman_note":"tick off-by-one-foreman-2026-10-06-18-08-53: OB-CI-001 recurrence escalated and fixed."}
