 {"id":"DF-OFF-BY-ONE-33","title":"user@host identifiers survive all PII surfaces (export, readonly API, corpus, site)","status":"complete","priority":"P1","complexity":3,"reasoning":"Dogfood 2026-10-09 (PII redaction round-trip, first consumer run of 8d3d7924). Injected 'Trace archived from kara@builder-machine. Contact ops-team@example.org.' into a community answer, imported -> exported -> re-imported across 3 scratch nodes and through a -readonly node: ops-team@example.org became <email> everywhere, but 'kara@builder-machine' passed through VERBATIM in the exported subtree (pre-solve-answers/.../evidence.md), the readonly /api/v1/problems/discover response, and every published surface that derives from it (data/answers.jsonl, data/answers/*.json, site/*.html). Root cause: personalEmailPattern (internal/export/git.go:538) requires a dotted TLD ([A-Z0-9.-]+\\.[A-Z]{2,}), so host-name domains (user@host, user@localhost, user@builder) escape it; there is no user@host fallback. Same class survives in the git-ready corpus: grep -rEo '\\b[A-Za-z0-9._-]+@[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\b' data/answers.jsonl currently returns hits. Fix direction: after the email regex, redact [A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9_-]+ (no dot) to <user-host> or <email>, in sanitizeCommonPII so export, SanitizePublicJSON, and the corpus regen all inherit it; add corpus-hygiene coverage for the dot-less form. Existing green checks miss it because check-public-pii.py mirrors the same dotted-TLD regex.","capability_tags":["privacy","export","api"],"updated_at":"2026-10-11T21:30:16Z","foreman_note":"verification-only close pending branch landing; ch:trace row=DF-OFF-BY-ONE-33 evidence=worktree:/home/kara/worktrees/off-by-one-DF-OFF-BY-ONE-33 witness=path@origin:9a07bc5d verdict=unavailable:gitreins-task-state-lost commit=9a07bc5d","worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/off-by-one-DF-OFF-BY-ONE-33","branch":"wt/DF-OFF-BY-ONE-33","worker_status":"complete","completed_at":"2026-10-11T23:05:00Z","commit_hash":"9a07bc5def16825012dccef96ce6cf13ab0e79aa","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"SKIP","worker_summary":"worker kimi-k3 commit 9a07bc5d; PII/corpus gates and full Go suite passed in isolated worktree; GitReins Tier 2 unavailable because task state was not visible after worker cleanup"}
