 {"id":"DF-OFF-BY-ONE-41","title":"[P2] required_tools degrade is invisible to the submitting agent: missing_tools=[...] appears only in the server log; no API surface reports the dropped tool","status":"complete","priority":"P2","type":"task","created_by":"off-by-one-dogfood","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:10:00Z","reasoning":"First real exercise of the documented required_tools path (README Request Fields: ['jq','parallel'] example, DF-39's OpenAPI schema). Submitted go-vet-copylocks-value-receiver-on-sync-mutex-20261013 (sub_ae14b0) with required_tools=['jq','parallel'] where parallel is NOT on the host. Degrade-gracefully contract held exactly as documented (internal/sandbox/tools.go:15): solve proceeded 2026-10-13T05:41:59Z, answer #4463 verified in 1m38s, jq resolved, parallel dropped. But the ONLY record of the drop is the server-log line 'WARN sandbox: could not resolve declared tools on host; solve will proceed without them missing_tools=[parallel]' (journalctl -u off-by-one 00:41:59). The submit 200 response, GET /api/v1/queue/{id} (pending and complete states), and the discover response all carry no tool field at all. A scripted agent that declared required_tools cannot learn its tool was unavailable except by reading the daemon's log, which a remote agent has no access to; the agent may wrongly assume its toolchain was provisioned. Fix direction: echo resolved/missing tool names back in the submit response and/or the queue status object (field names matching the OpenAPI schema fixed in DF-39). Evidence: docs/dogfood/2026-10-13-tools-integration.md.","worker_status":"pass","exit_code":0,"commit_hash":"c18f48b8","completed_at":"2026-10-13T22:55:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T22:55:00Z","worker_summary":"required_tools now surfaced as resolved_tools/missing_tools ([] never null) on submit response + queue objects, persisted on queue entries (schema +2 cols); openapi.yaml + README/docs updated; 720+/-17 across 13 files; full short suite 15 pkgs ok.","guard_resul