 {"id":"DF-OFF-BY-ONE-37-R2","title":"[P2] RECURRENCE of DF-37 (answer-corpus arm) \u2014 the dedup 409 still returns submission_id:\"\" when the hit is a VERIFIED ANSWER rather than a queue entry, so the documented \"poll the existing submission\" contract is unsatisfiable on that arm","status":"complete","priority":"P2","complexity":2,"depends_on":[],"blocks":[],"primary_model":null,"primary_provider":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"reasoning":"DOGFOOD 2026-10-20 (run 19) \u2014 scratch instance built from HEAD fda8b3a2, seeded 2785 classes.\n\nREPRO (verbatim; the tuple must match the corpus answer stored env=docker/lang=go/version=latest):\n  $ curl -s -X POST :18801/api/v1/problems/submit -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n      -d '{\"problem_class\":\"go-http-validation-auth-input\",\"environment\":\"docker\",\"language\":\"go\",\n           \"version\":\"latest\",\"cadence\":\"post-debug\",\"description\":\"dup arm\"}'\n    HTTP 409\n    {\"submission_id\":\"\",\"problem_class\":\"go-http-validation-auth-input\",\"status\":\"deduplicated\",\n     \"position\":0,\"estimated_time\":\"\",\"existing_solutions\":1,\"related_problems\":[...7 ids...],\n     \"resolved_tools\":[],\"missing_tools\":[]}\n  Repeat -> byte-identical: submission_id is \"\" on both, so the second call could not even point at the first.\n\nDOCS PROMISE (quoted verbatim):\n  README.md:217-220 \u2014 \"A submission is deduplicated against the queue and the verified-answer corpus ...\n    409 with \"status\": \"deduplicated\" and the existing submission_id (the same id the first submit returned)\"\n  docs/api-reference.md:73 \u2014 \"When that tuple is already queued/in progress or already has a verified answer,\n    no second job is created: the response carries status deduplicated and the EXISTING submission_id ...\n    with its queue position\"\n  The queue-entry arm DOES satisfy it (verified in-browser this run: second SPA submit of the same tuple \u2192\n  409 {\"submission_id\":\"sub_fd245d\",\"status\":\"deduplicated\",\"position\":1}), which is precisely what DF-37's\n  2026-10-13 fix covered.\n\nWHY THE ARM CANNOT BE SATISFIED AS WRITTEN: internal/api/handlers.go:340-355 stamps the existing queue\nentry's id when ErrDuplicate comes from findPendingDuplicate (queue.go:254-261); the corpus-answer arm\nreturns ErrDuplicate with NO entry (queue.go:266-272), so there is no id to stamp. The response carries\nexisting_solutions:1 but no pointer to the answer and no next-step hint \u2014 a scripted Muster consumer that\nfollows the docs is left with an id that resolves to nothing (GET /api/v1/queue/ \u2192 404/empty).","fix_direction":"Pick one and make it explicit on the wire:\n(a) carry a resolvable pointer for the answered arm \u2014 e.g. answer_id/class + a discover hint (found/answer),\n    or a synthesized stable id that GET /api/v1/queue/{id} resolves; or\n(b) document the answered arm in README + docs/api-reference (\"submission_id: \"\" + existing_solutions > 0\n    = already answered, call POST /api/v1/problems/discover\"), and add a distinguishing field\n    (reason: \"queued\" | \"answered\") so the two 409 arms are not byte-identical.\nAcceptance: a scripted consumer can act on either dedup arm without reading the source; a regression test\ncovers the CORPUS arm (the existing test covers only the queue arm).","capability_tags":["api","docs","contract","dogfood","recurrence"],"created_by":null,"created_at":"2026-10-20T11:13:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T22:26:37Z","worker_status":"complete","attempts":0,"exit_code":null,"commit_hash":"33ad3dd48007d516346ef821ce11df3f79ddaa93","files_changed":[],"lines_added":0,"lines_removed":0,"guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Worker commit 33ad3dd48007d516346ef821ce11df3f79ddaa93. Independent verification: gofmt clean; go test ./internal/api/... -count=1 PASS; go build ./... PASS; go vet ./... PASS; go test ./... -short -p 1 -count=1 -timeout 120s PASS; 