-{"id":"DF-OFF-BY-ONE-54","title":"[P2] The Submit form's fixed environment vocabulary (Any/dev/staging/prod/ci/local) cannot express the values the corpus and its own docs use (docker, linux), so the documented \"already has a verified answer \u2192 409\" dedup is unreachable from the SPA: a UI user re-queues a solve of an answered class while the panel says \"1 existing solution found.\"","status":"complete","priority":"P2","complexity":3,"depends_on":[],"blocks":[],"primary_model":null,"primary_provider":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"reasoning":"DOGFOOD 2026-10-20 (run 19) \u2014 driven in a real browser against a HEAD instance seeded with the bundled\ncorpus (2785 classes / 2883 answers), with window.fetch instrumented to capture the wire bodies.\n\nEVIDENCE:\n  Explore (same build): drilling the class go-http-validation-auth-input renders\n    class -> env \"docker\" -> lang \"go\" -> version \"latest\" -> answer (VERIFIED, detail pane 4285 chars).\n  Submit form: document.querySelectorAll('#submit-env option') ->\n    '', 'dev', 'staging', 'prod', 'ci', 'local'      (no docker, no linux)\n    version is free text; language offers go/python/rust/typescript/javascript/java/c/cpp.\n  UI submit #1 (class above, env=local, lang=go, version empty) ->\n    HTTP 200 {\"submission_id\":\"sub_fd245d\",\"status\":\"queued\",\"position\":3,\"estimated_time\":\"1m30s\",\n              \"existing_solutions\":1,...}\n    panel: \"QUEUED ... Queue position: #3 ... 1 existing solution found.\" -> a NEW solve is queued for a\n    class that already holds a verified answer served by discover in 0.68 ms.\n  UI submit #2 (identical tuple) -> HTTP 409 dedup, panel \"DEDUPLICATED ... Already queued (sub_fd245d),\n    position 1 \u2014 this problem was already solved or is already in the queue.\" (DF-43's fix holds.)\n  Docs/API use env values the form cannot express: README's submit example uses \"environment\": \"linux\";\n  the corpus answers store env=docker/lang=go/version=latest \u2014 so the form's tuple can never equal the\n  corpus tuple, and the corpus arm of the documented dedup is unreachable from the product's own UI.\n\nIMPACT: the SPA is the human entry point of a system whose stated economics are \"convert idle compute\ncycles\". A user is told an answer already exists and the lab still spends a solve re-answering it; the\nresulting confusion (\"why did dedup not fire?\") lands on the user, not the docs.","fix_direction":"Make the environment input able to express reality: free-text with a datalist seeded from the taxonomy's\nactual env values (docker/linux/... appear there), or at minimum add the observed vocabulary. Optionally\nalso dedup by class when existing_solutions > 0 and hand back the answer pointer (discover link) instead of\nqueueing a duplicate solve. Acceptance: submitting an already-answered class from the UI reaches the\n409/answered path, or the form can express the corpus/docs tuple.","capability_tags":["ui","api","dedup","docs","dogfood"],"created_by":null,"created_at":"2026-10-20T11:13:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T22:12:00Z","worker_status":"complete","attempts":0,"exit_code":null,"commit_hash":"3cd4d5c850e275f8f2da02a5648e245c79d18fd1","files_changed":[],"lines_added":0,"lines_removed":0,"guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"SKIP","worker_summary":"Worker added docker and linux to web/js/submit.js; go test ./internal/api/ passed; GitReins Tier-2 PASS at .gitreins/history/2026-10-21/5d4cf7c9/verdict.json bound to 3cd4d5c850e275f8f2da02a5648e245c79d18fd1.","foreman_note":"Tick off-by-one-foreman-2026-10-21-21-32-28: serial worker commit landed, trace binding follow-up landed, pushed with remote parity 0/0. Exact-head CI was queued at close; not claimed green.","blocked_reason":null,"review_notes":null,"completed_at":"2026-10-21T22:12:00Z","blocked_since":null,"detail":{"fingerprint":"4165f250b2b3ed86527977a375f380eee1f5e7fcec6662e9146e3bcf6ed9fbbc","evidence":[{"run_id":"5d4cf7c9","ts":"20