 {"id":"DF-OFF-BY-ONE-55","title":"[P3] The board-lint pre-commit hook installed in this repo is INERT: a global core.hooksPath (/home/kara/.hermes/hooks) overrides $GIT_DIR/hooks, so git never runs .git/hooks/pre-commit \u2014 the board's duplicate-id / dangling-dep gate is dead in exactly the checkout that advertises it (BT-053-ROLLOUT row)","status":"complete","priority":"P3","complexity":2,"depends_on":[],"blocks":[],"primary_model":null,"primary_provider":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"reasoning":"DOGFOOD 2026-10-20 (run 19) \u2014 found while landing this run's own commit, verified by git's own\npath resolution (no experiment needed).\n\nEVIDENCE:\n  $ git config --get core.hooksPath\n    /home/kara/.hermes/hooks\n  $ git rev-parse --git-path hooks/pre-commit\n    /home/kara/.hermes/hooks/pre-commit        <-- what git actually consults\n  $ ls -l .git/hooks/pre-commit\n    -rwxr-xr-x ... .git/hooks/pre-commit      <-- carries the boardctl board-lint managed block\n  $ head -30 /home/kara/.hermes/hooks/pre-commit\n    #!/usr/bin/env bash ... REPO_ROOT=... ; /home/kara/gitreins/.venv/bin/python -m gitreins guard; exit $?\n    (no chaining to $GIT_DIR/hooks/pre-commit)\n  $ git commit -F <msg>   # this run's commit a2784353, docs+board only\n    guard log: .gitreins/logs/guard-20261020T111645.392968Z.log -> secrets clean, go_build/go_tests skipped\n    (the gitreins guard ran; no board-lint step exists in the effective hook at all)\n\nMECHANISM: when core.hooksPath is set, git looks for hooks ONLY there \u2014 $GIT_DIR/hooks is ignored. So the\nboard-lint hook that `boardctl install` wrote into .git/hooks (recorded as complete by\nBT-053-ROLLOUT-2026-09-28, \"board-lint pre-commit hook: installed\") never executes in this checkout, and\nneither would any other repo-local hook the fleet installs. The board's own protection against duplicate\nids / dangling depends_on (the tick contract calls a duplicate id a board-lint ERROR that blocks EVERY\ncommit in the repo) is therefore inert exactly where it is advertised as installed.\n\nIMPACT: a duplicate-id or dangling-dep commit from any lane writing this board sails through; the failure\nsurfaces later as a repo-wide commit block or as a silently unreachable row. Nothing reports the gap \u2014\n`boardctl validate` is a manual/CI invocation, not a commit gate, and the effective hook prints nothing\nabout the board.\n\nNOTE (not a claim about boardctl's intent): the global hook is a fleet-wide install, so the same\noverride applies to every repo in the fleet that boardctl installed into.","fix_direction":"Fix lives in boardctl's install path (cross-project: this board only records it).\n`boardctl install` must write the board-lint block into the EFFECTIVE hook path \u2014 resolve it with\n`git rev-parse --git-path hooks/pre-commit` (or install the block where core.hooksPath points and chain the\nrepo's own hooks from there) \u2014 and must detect the override at install time and either adapt or fail with a\nnamed remedy instead of reporting a successful install. Acceptance: in a repo whose core.hooksPath is set\nglobally, a commit that introduces a duplicate task id (or a dangling depends_on) is still BLOCKED, or the\ninstall names the override and refuses to claim success. Add the case to boardctl's own install test.","capability_tags":["board","process","tooling","dogfood"],"created_by":null,"created_at":"2026-10-20T11:17:39Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T23:00:00Z","worker_status":"foreman-verify-only","attempts":0,"exit_code":null,"commit_hash":"75420a1fe000bff20d8ee5e6da96d75f1b6972ac","files_changed":[],"lines_added":0,"lines_removed":0,"guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"RED: existing runner-local RLIMIT_AS OOM; tracked by INT-CI-002","worker_summary":"STATUS: complete / TIER: T3 / EVIDENCE: scripts/tests/install-hooks-selftest.sh; .gitreins/history/2026-10-25/cb85b1bd/verdict.json / ch:trace row=DF-OFF-BY-ONE-55 spec=.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl wave=