UCCESS, all 6 jobs success including 'Corpus host-path hygiene'.\n  - the target itself passes natively at HEAD: `python3 scripts/tests/generate_static_site_redaction_test.py` -> Ran 15 tests ... OK, rc=0; golangci-lint full run -> 0 issues.\n\nWHY IT IS STILL A FINDING: the workflow installs a Python dependency with a bare `pip install` and no actions/setup-python, so the gate only works where the runner's Python packaging policy happens to allow system installs. On a stock Ubuntu image (act's catthehacker image, a self-hosted runner, or a future runner-image change) the job fails closed BEFORE the redaction test executes: the OB-GAP-093 gate is then absent while the workflow still looks like it enforces it. The act leg is also the harness's own CI signal, so this step makes the ci-pass act leg red on every cycle for this repo.","fix_direction":"Make the step runner-portable: either add `actions/setup-python` (pinned version) before it, or install through the interpreter with an explicit escape \u2014 `python3 -m pip install --break-system-packages markdown` \u2014 or vendor the dependency so no install happens at all. Acceptance: `act -P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest -j corpus-hygiene` exits 0 on the pinned image AND hosted CI stays green on the same commit; the redaction test's own 15 tests keep passing.","capability_tags":["ci","workflow","portability","qa"],"created_by":"off-by-one-qa","created_at":"2026-10-21T11:50:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T23:30:23Z","worker_status":"complete","attempts":0,"exit_code":0,"commit_hash":"b4997e5d017b9db93efa1208220635e00c14a023","files_changed":[".github/workflows/ci.yml"],"lines_added":1,"lines_removed":1,"guard_result":{"status":"pass","details":"tier1 DEGRADED PASS (yaml-only staging; go skips legitimate); merged-tree verify: go build OK, YAML parse OK, site-redaction-selftest 15 tests OK, go test -short 15 ok / 0 FAIL, no bare 'pip install markdown' remains"},"ci_result":{"status":"pending","details":"push