+{"id":"QA-OFF-BY-ONE-5-R2","title":"[P3] RECURRENCE of QA-OFF-BY-ONE-5 \u2014 chaos-disconnect still yields NO signal on off-by-one (disc.log 0 bytes with rc=0) for the 3rd consecutive cycle, so the network cut is never exercised","status":"complete","priority":"P3","complexity":2,"depends_on":[],"blocks":[],"primary_model":null,"primary_provider":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"reasoning":"Tick %s \u2014 %s.\n\nEVIDENCE this cycle (agent 0d6df5a6, per-cell logs harvested before destroy):\n  cell chaos-disconnect UNVERIFIED \"disc.log is EMPTY (0 bytes) or never-ran (no-test-path marker) -- the suite produced NO output, so the network cut was NEVER exercised; rc=0 is not a disconnect result (QA-WARPFS-17; QA-BUNKER-29 vacuity class)\"  \u2014 disc.log = 0 bytes.\n  Same agent, same tree: the native suite DID produce output \u2014 native.log lists 17 packages ok (ci-pass OK, rc=0) and res.log lists the same 17 packages ok under the 3G cap (chaos-resource PASS). So the empty disc.log is not 'a silent repo'.\n\nEXACT INVOCATION (read from the battery's generated qa-run.sh on the agent):\n  ( HTTP_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:9 HTTPS_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:9 ALL_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:9 PATH=\"$HOME/tools/go/bin:$PATH\" GOFLAGS=-mod=mod GOPROXY=off GOSUMDB=off GOTOOLCHAIN=local timeout $disc_window bash -c \"$native_cmd\" ) > disc.log 2>&1   [native_cmd = `go test ./... -count=1`]\n  -> disc_rc=0 AND a 0-byte log = the QA-BUNKER-30 fingerprint (a command that never ran / expanded empty): an rc=0 must carry a suite artifact, and a go suite that ran always prints per-package lines.\n\nOFF-BATTERY CONTRAST (dev box, worktree at HEAD %s, same env + same command): the arm DOES emit output \u2014 'go: go.mod requires go >= 1.26.9 (running go 1.26.5; GOTOOLCHAIN=local)', rc=1, 72 bytes (the harness even has a dedicated classifier arm, go_toolchain_floor_failure, for that shape). So the invocation shape is capable of producing a log; the agent-side 0-byte/rc=0 r