ne since 2026-10-23, normalized to complete. Fresh seed 8.7s: 3242 classes / 3242 distinct created_at (pre-fix report: 60 distinct for 2856 classes, all inside the seed run). Class serde-json-validator-jsonschema = corpus date 2026-07-25 01:10:08 with answers 2026-07-25 01:10:08 + 2026-10-01 07:20:47. Re-seed: 0 classes created, stamps unchanged. AC text rewritten to drop the stale numeric ids (class_id=112 is now garbled-circuit-evaluator; the described answers belong to class 89).","detail":{"evidence":[{"run_id":"df58a001","ts":"2026-11-21T12:10:20Z"}]}}
 {"id":"DF-OFF-BY-ONE-59","title":"[P3] SPA version chip renders \"vv0.2.0\": web/js/app.js:175 does elVersion.textContent = 'v' + j.version while GET /health already returns version \"v0.2.0\", so the header chip shows a doubled prefix on every deployment (the REVIEW-OB-021 fix wired the chip but the two halves were never composed in a browser)","status":"complete","priority":"P3","complexity":1,"type":"task","created_by":"dogfood-off-by-one-2026-10-23-1243","created_at":"2026-10-23T12:56:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T12:56:53Z","capability_tags":["web","ui","health"],"reasoning":"Observed in a real browser on the released v0.2.0 binary (port 18801): `GET /health` -> {\"status\":\"ok\",\"uptime\":\"4s\",\"version\":\"v0.2.0\"} and the rendered chip text (document.getElementById('status-version').textContent) is 'vv0.2.0'. Source: web/index.html:88 ships the placeholder 'v0.0.0' and web/js/app.js:175 sets `elVersion.textContent = 'v' + j.version`. The binary stamps its version WITH the leading v (`off-by-one --version` -> 'off-by-one v0.2.0'), so the JS prepend doubles it. REVIEW-OB-021 closed by making /health carry the version; the composing step was never driven in a browser, which is why the row closed green while the chip is visibly wrong. Fix is one line either in app.js (use j.version verbatim) or in the /health payload (bare semver) - pick one and pin the rendered string.","acceptance_criteria":"With the built binary serving, a browser (or `curl -s / | grep status-version` plus the JS path) shows the chip textContent EXACTLY 'v0.2.0' (one leading v): `node -e \"const j={version:'v0.2.0'}\"` style composition test or a jsdom/playwright assertion on #status-version === 'v0.2.0' passes, and the same assertion fails if /health's version is bare '0.2.0' without a matching app.js change (i.e. the two sides are consistent, not accidentally green).\n\nEvidence verifiable via cited probes.","acceptance":"With the built binary serving (`/tmp/ob59 -db /tmp/ob59.db -port 18996` after seeding), the composed chip must carry exactly one leading v: run `V=$(curl -s http://127.0.0.1:18996/health | jq -r .version); case \"$V\" in v*) grep -c \"'v' + j.version\" web/js/app.js;; *) echo 0;; esac` and it must output 0 (never both halves prefixing), `grep -c 'status-version' web/js/app.js` returns at least 1 and `grep -c 'id=\"status-version\"' web/index.html` returns 1, and the expected end state is a rendered chip textContent of v0.2.0, never vv0.2.0, i.e. `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:18996/health | jq -r .version` and the app.js assignment agree on who adds the v.","worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"8ae250b7","completed_at":"2026-10-24T02:02:00Z","foreman_note":"tick 2026-10-24-01-57-41: foreman-direct (Exception 3 UI); web/js/app.js:175 now checks startsWith(\"v\") before prepending; guard DEGRADED PASS (JS-only, no Go staged); pushed 8ae250b7; CI green (5/5 success)"}
-{"id":"DF-OFF-BY-ONE-60","title":"[P3] README's 'Install from a release' snippet hardcodes V=v0.1.1, so following the documented first command verbatim installs an artifact two releases behind v0.2.0 that lacks the dedup answered-arm contract and the /health version field","status":"complete","priority":"P3","complexity":1,"type":"task","created_by":"dogfood-off-by-one-2026-10-23-1243","created_at":"2026-10-23T12:56:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-24T16:32:21Z","capability_tags":["docs","release","install"],"reasoning":"README.md's install-from-a-release block opens with `V=v0.1.1` (the release download recipe) while v0.2.0 is the current release (tag eabb6741, published 2026-10-23T05:26Z, 5 assets). Driven for real: downloaded off-by-one-v0.1.1-linux-amd64 (HTTP 200, 16958123 bytes), ran it against the same seeded graph -> `GET /health` = {\"status\":\"ok\",\"uptime\":\"6s\"} (NO version field, so the SPA chip stays at its v0.0.0 placeholder) and the answered-arm dedup POST returns {\"submission_id\":\"\",\"status\":\"deduplicated\",\"position\":0,\"existing_solutions\":12,...} with NO reason and NO next_action - the pre-33ad3dd4 shape, i.e. the user gets an unpollable 409 with no pointer to discover. Same request on v0.2.0 returns reason:\"answered\" + next_action:\"POST /api/v1/problems/discover\". So the documented install path silently ships the older contract, and a reader cannot tell which fixes they have. Fix: derive V from the latest release (or a placeholder the user must fill) and keep the snippet's version current at each cut - this is the doc that must not go stale.","acceptance_criteria":"`grep -n 'V=v' README.md` shows no hardcoded release older than the current tag (or the snippet uses a clearly-marked placeholder), and a guard/probe resolves the latest release tag from the GitHub API and fails when README's pinned V is not that tag: `gh release view --json tagName -q .tagName` equals the V in the install block. Running the block verbatim resolves an artifact whose `--version` equals the latest tag.\n\nEvidence verifiable via cited probes.","acceptance":"`grep -m1 '^V=' README.md` prints the install block's pinned version and it must equal the live latest release tag: `test \"$(grep -m1 '^V=' README.md | cut -d= -f2)\" = \"$(curl -s https://api.github.com/repos/totalwindupflightsystems/off-by-one/releases/latest | jq -r .tag_name)\"` exits 0, and `grep -c 'V=v0.1.1' README.md` returns 0 so no documented install command pins an artifact older than the current release. PASS = equality test exits 0 and the stale pin count is 0.","worker_status":"complete","worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/off-by-one-DF-OFF-BY-ONE-60","branch":"wt/DF-OFF-BY-ONE-60","commit_hash":"65585b4d3683a927efb630afd50b9323d427d480","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"ch:trace row=DF-OFF-BY-ONE-60 spec=.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl#DF-OFF-BY-ONE-60 wave=.coding-hermes/waves/off-by-one-foreman-2026-10-24-16-01-24.json#slot-1 test=README.md::release-version-equality doc=README.md prompt=/tmp/ob-60-brief.txt evidence=.gitreins/history/2026-10-24/2bb80546/verdict.json witness=github:releases/latest verdict=.gitreins/history/2026-10-24/2bb80546/verdict.json commit=65585b4d3683a927efb630afd50b9323d427d480 memory=/project/off-by-one/status STATUS: complete TIER: T3 EVIDENCE: README V=v0.2.0 equals GitHub latest; stale V=v0.1.1 count 0; GitReins Tier1+Tier2 PASS.","foreman_note":"Merged 82ffd2c8 via 18ad8e65; verified on merged tree; initial worker-branch judge e5df1f0c was stale-base and correctly superseded by main-tree PASS 2bb80546.","completed_at":"2026-10-24T16:30:00Z","detail":{"evidence":[{"run_id":".gitreins/history/2026-10-24/2bb80546/verdict.json","ts":"2026-10-24T16:32:21Z"}]}}
-{"id":"DF-OFF-BY-ONE-61","title":"[P4] A healthy startup with an empty queue logs an error-shaped line every time: 'cron: deferral stamp: peek queue head failed: queue: not found (continuing)' - the same normal-resting-state-reads-as-error class as DF-47, on the released v0.2.0 artifact","status":"complete","priority":"P4","complexity":1,"type":"task","created_by":"dogfood-off-by-one-2026-10-23-1243","created_at":"2026-10-23T12:56:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-24T16:32:21Z","capability_tags":["observability","logging","cron"],"reasoning":"Observed at first start of the released v0.2.0 binary on a freshly seeded DB with an EMPTY queue and nothing broken: serve.log line `2026/10/23 07:53:03 cron: deferral stamp: peek queue head failed: queue: not found (continuing)` \u2014 emitted at startup, before any submission existed. The same line reappears on every restart with an empty queue (reproduced on the 07:55 cold-start restart; not reproduced when a submission is pending). 'queue: not found' is the documented representation of an empty queue (GET /api/v1/queue -> {\"entries\":[],\"total\":0}, not an error), so an operator reading logs for faults is told a healthy idle node failed. This is the same class DF-47 fixed for the load-gate line ('cron: deferred - host busy (load): used X / threshold 4.000'); the empty-queue arm was left behind. Fix: treat an empty head as the normal case (debug-level or 'queue empty, no deferral stamp needed'), keep a real peek failure as an error.","acceptance_criteria":"Start the binary against a freshly seeded DB with no submissions and grep the log: `grep -c 'queue: not found' <serve.log>` is 0 while `grep -ci 'queue empty\\|no deferral stamp' <serve.log>` shows the normal-state line, AND a forced failure (e.g. closing the queue table / passing an unwritable db) still logs a line containing 'peek queue head failed'.\n\nEvidence verifiable via cited probes.","acceptance":"Build and start against a freshly seeded DB with an empty queue: `go build -o /tmp/ob61 ./cmd/off-by-one && /tmp/ob61 -db /tmp/ob61.db seed >/dev/null && (/tmp/ob61 -db /tmp/ob61.db -port 18995 -load-threshold -1 >/tmp/ob61-serve.log 2>&1 &) && sleep 5`, then `grep -c 'queue: not found' /tmp/ob61-serve.log` returns 0 and `grep -ci 'peek queue head failed' /tmp/ob61-serve.log` returns 0 on a healthy idle node, while the real-failure path is retained: `grep -c 'peek queue head failed' internal/cron/loop.go` returns 1 and `grep -c 'ingest.ErrNotFound' internal/cron/loop.go` returns at least 1, and `go test ./internal/cron/ -count=1` exits 0.","worker_status":"complete","worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/off-by-one-DF-OFF-BY-ONE-61","branch":"wt/DF-OFF-BY-ONE-61","commit_hash":"65585b4d3683a927efb630afd50b9323d427d480","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"ch:trace row=DF-OFF-BY-ONE-61 spec=.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl#DF-OFF-BY-ONE-61 wave=.coding-hermes/waves/off-by-one-foreman-2026-10-24-16-01-24.json#slot-2 test=internal/cron/loop_test.go::empty-queue-deferral doc=none:not-a-doc-task prompt=/tmp/ob-61-brief.txt evidence=.gitreins/history/2026-10-24/e329bc5d/verdict.json witness=live:localhost:8766 verdict=.gitreins/history/2026-10-24/e329bc5d/verdict.json commit=65585b4d3683a927efb630afd50b9323d427d480 memory=/project/off-by-one/status STATUS: complete TIER: T3 EVIDENCE: focused cron tests, build, vet and merged-tree GitReins Tier1+Tier2 PASS; ErrNotFound normal line and real failure branch both verified.","foreman_note":"Merged c98b1cd9 via 65585b4d; merged-tree GitReins verdict e329bc5d PASS; live binary refresh remains required because Go source changed.","completed_at":"2026-10-24T16:30:00Z","detail":{"evidence":[{"run_id":".gitreins/history/2026-10-24/e329bc5d/verdict.json","ts":"2026-10-24T16:32:21Z"}]}}
-{"id":"PERF-OFF-BY-ONE-1","title":"[P3] seed's install step pays a per-statement fsync: 44.7-70.5s on ext4 vs 3.4-3.7s on tmpfs for the same corpus and binary (17x) \u2014 not the link scan","status":"complete","priority":"P3","complexity":2,"type":"task","created_by":"dogfood-off-by-one-2026-10-23-1243b","created_at":"2026-10-23T13:06:33Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T19:00:00Z","capability_tags":["perf","sqlite","seed","install"],"reasoning":"Measured on the RELEASED v0.2.0 artifact (asset sha256 c2638ce9\u2026a013fc) against a depth-1 clone of HEAD ea5b963a, host /tmp on /dev/nvme0n1p2 (ext4), corpus = data/answers/*.json (2856 files).\n\nEXACT COMMAND (control and treatment are the same command; only the -db target differs):\n  /usr/bin/time -f 'WALL=%e user=%U sys=%S' ../off-by-one-v0.2.0-linux-amd64 seed -db <DB>\n\next4 arm: 44.70s (user 6.06 sys 1.31) \u00b7 59.53s (6.53/1.43) \u00b7 64.21s (6.81/1.41) \u00b7 70.51s under strace (9.88/11.17)\ntmpfs arm (-db /dev/shm/<fresh>.db): 3.72s (3.41/0.40) \u00b7 3.39s (3.10/0.39)\nEvery arm prints the identical result line: files=2856; classes=2856 created / 0 existing; answers=2955 created / 1530 skipped; edges=12872 created.\n\u21d2 17x wall difference, ~56s of it added by disk writes. CPU is the SAME work in both arms (~3.4s tmpfs vs ~8.2s ext4), so the per-class link scan cannot own the seconds: that scan runs in BOTH arms.\n\nSyscall census (strace -f -c on an ext4 arm): 9136 fsync, 253070 pwrite64, 130177 nanosleep, 29361 futex, 3208 tgkill \u2014 top entry futex 36.95s.\n\nHot path (read-only inspection, no code changed):\n- internal/seed/seed.go:91 \u2014 `for _, ent := range entries { seedFile(...) }`; internal/seed/seed.go:127 calls store.UpsertProblemClass per file.\n- `grep -c -E 'Begin|Commit' internal/seed/seed.go` = 0 \u2014 no transaction wraps the load, so every INSERT autocommits.\n- internal/graph/store.go:152 \u2014 DSN `_pragma=journal_mode(WAL)&_pragma=busy_timeout(5000)`; each autocommitted statement in WAL pays its own fsync.\n- internal/graph/linker.go \u2014 LinkAllSimilar writes one INSERT per edge (12872 edges) through the same autocommit path.\n\nUser impact: this is the headline install step of README \"Install from a release\"; the user waits ~1 minute for ~4s of work before the catalog exists, and the README's \"zero to a working catalog in under a minute\" claim then depends on host I/O luck (measured envelopes on this box: 52s with the 44.7s seed; >70s with the 64-70s seeds).\n\nRelationship to the earlier dogfood entry for this tick (docs/dogfood/2026-10-23-release-artifact-integration.md \u00a7Performance): its numbers are reproduced here (it recorded 58.97s) but its ATTRIBUTION is not \u2014 it assigned the residual to \"the per-class link scan already tracked as OB-GAP-073\" and concluded \"nothing a user would feel\". OB-GAP-073 is closed, and the tmpfs control shows the link scan is not the cost; the cost is per-statement fsync on the install path. A one-minute first-install wait is user-noticeable, so this is filed as a PERF row rather than left as a note.\n\nFix shape (foreman's call): wrap the whole seed load (classes + answers + edges, including LinkAllSimilar) in ONE transaction, or in per-chunk batches with a single fsync each; keep the loader idempotent. Expected: ext4 seed lands in the tmpfs arm's 3-4s range; fsync count drops from 9136 to a handful.","acceptance_criteria":"A fresh seed on the same corpus and binary completes in <=10s wall on ext4: `/usr/bin/time -f 'WALL=%e user=%U sys=%S' ./off-by-one seed -db /tmp/seed-perf-a.db` (fresh DB path) reports WALL <= 10, against the recorded baseline 44.70/59.53/64.21/70.51s and the tmpfs control 3.39/3.72s; the post-fix ext4 arm must land within ~1s of the same command run with -db /dev/shm/seed-perf-b.db.\n\nThe fsync count drops by two orders of magnitude: `strace -f -c -o /tmp/